Rule 6 (when x is 1D, its length must match the size of y along the integration axis)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : int} |= if ndim(v_2) = 1 then (if v_3 ≥ 0 then shape(v_2, 0) = shape(v_1, v_3) else shape(v_2, 0) = shape(v_1, v_3 + ndim(v_1)))
>>
Rule 7 (when x has the same dimensionality as y, their shapes must match along all dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_2) = ndim(v_1) then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) = shape(v_1, i)
>>
Rule 8 (sample spacing dx when given as a tensor must be a scalar)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 0
>>
Rule 9 (sample spacing dx must not be zero)
